3. Validation Standards : Under the FDCPA, you are required to provide specific evidence substantiating the debt. This includes, but is not limited to : Original creditors name and contact information. 
A signed agreement or contract obligating me to repay the debt. 
An itemized account history detailing the principal, fees, interest, and any other charges. 

Until proper validation is provided, including evidence of ownership and documentation substantiating the alleged balance, I dispute this debt in its entirety. I further reiterate my previous request to cease all communication, in compliance with my rights under the FDCPA. 

